    "source_detail": "Finstack Quant canonical credit pricing calculation on deterministic synthetic market inputs Canonical typed market inputs are supplied directly; the pricing tolerance contract is preserved. Re-baselined 2026-06-09 after intentional tranche pricer corrections (2026-06-09 quant review Majors 4-6): accrual-on-default complement fix ((1-f)*dEL), discount-curve-axis relative discounting from as_of, and senior-side recovery amortization of the detachment. Formula self-test goldens track the canonical calculation; tolerance contract unchanged. Re-baselined 2026-07-11 after the seasoned premium-accrual boundary correction. Re-pinned expected outputs on 2026-07-23 for 0.6.0 release prep (small calibrate/price round-trip drift). Re-baselined 2026-09-04 from a replayable CDS par-spread calibration so cs01 measures canonical quote-space rebootstrap risk rather than a direct intensity shift. Re-baselined 2026-09-18: commit 413953021 replaced the tranche factor quadrature with partitioned adaptive Simpson under an explicit absolute integration budget, and commit 82937c4ea's large-homogeneous-pool shortcut (which mis-priced index-sized pools) was reverted so the exact conditional binomial applies at every pool size. The Hull-White (2004) Table 7 par-spread assertions are unchanged and pass; only the internal deterministic pins are re-captured.",
